From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mod_public_ip: correct DNS answers, IPv4 and IPv6, more providers
Requires: 001-check-fixes-ip-version-outbound-check

- DNS answers: every record of the authority and additional sections
  was read as an answer (the number of records was the largest of
  ANCOUNT, NSCOUNT, ARCOUNT), so addresses of name servers were shown
  as the public IP. IPv6 addresses were shortened wrongly
  (2001:db8:10::1 became 2001:db8:1::1). Now only the answer section is
  read, names with compression are skipped, RCODE is checked and IPv6
  is written by RFC 5952.
- The DNS socket takes the family of the IP version, so an IPv6 request
  to a server given by name goes over IPv6.
- HTTP providers: the IP version (option qtype) applies to them too
  (curl --ipv4/--ipv6; default IPv4). qtype 2 makes an IPv4 and an IPv6
  request and shows both addresses.
- curl got only --connect-timeout (now also --max-time), the proxy
  without user and password, and the URL in double quotes. The proxy
  string of the daemon is used (with authentication), values are
  single-quoted.
- More HTTP(S) providers; a provider with url6 uses a separate address
  for IPv6. Provider "custom" with the options custom_url and
  custom_url6. An answer is accepted as the address alone, a line
  ip=..., a JSON field "ip" or a JSON string.

